<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middle Assyrian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Middle Assyrian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> was the phase of Assyrian history that began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashur-uballit-i">Ashur-uballit I</a> asserted independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> in the fourteenth century BCE. Assyria expanded across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and fought major rivals such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. It declined after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> upheavals before the Neo-Assyrian revival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/middle-assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="Middle Assyrian Empire" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Near_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A9dio-assyrien.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
